Run from line N (AUTO_RUN N) skips the lines before N and runs line N.

lines.ngc puts one (DEBUG,Lk) on each line k and an END line the start line
never passes; for every N the messages up to END must be exactly L<N>.. — the
start line used to be executed into the discard sink, so a run began one line
late.

blend.ngc sets G64 on line 1 and runs from line 2, after an MDI G61. The
skipped G64 reached the canon but never the trajectory planner, which kept
exact stop (max X 5.0; after a fresh start, its 0.001 in boot tolerance gave
4.999). The planner must get the modal blending mode the skipped lines left,
so the corner blends (max X well under 5; 3.725 here).
